@lang pt
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cp-dominio`
IMPORT `cp-pena`

-- Independent test pass, ta-g3 (arts. 155 to 212): what the cp-ind-g3-*
-- modules share. No directive here. The expected values live in the modules
-- that import this, one directive per case of
-- ~/.claude/br-penal-oracle/cases/ta-g3.json, written from the source text
-- before the encoding existed.

§ `Testes independentes de ta-g3 — o que os módulos partilham`

-- The cases were written against the compiled text as amended through Lei nº
-- 15.517/2026 (DOU 23.9.2026), and state no date. Every fact is dated after
-- the last law in force in the range, so the text in the source is the one
-- that governs it.
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg:en the date every independent case is set on, after the last amending law
`a data dos casos independentes` MEANS YMD 2026 9 28

-- A case states a penalty as the preceito prints it: species, the two bounds
-- and the fine's conjunction. The encoding's `Pena cominada` also carries
-- whether the violence's penalty is added; a case that states that asks it
-- separately, so the comparison reads only the four.
GIVEN pc IS A `Pena cominada`
      e  IS AN `Espécie de pena privativa de liberdade`
      mn IS A Duração
      mx IS A Duração
      m  IS A `Cominação da multa`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the prescribed penalty has this species, these bounds and this fine
`a pena confere com` pc e mn mx m MEANS
        pc's `espécie` EQUALS e
    AND pc's `mínimo` EQUALS mn
    AND pc's `máximo` EQUALS mx
    AND pc's multa EQUALS m
